# A function may not REBIND a variable captured from an enclosing function (write-through closures are
# not allowed, so closures stay soundly inlinable). Caught at compile time, before the program runs.
# The idiomatic alternatives: return the new value, or capture a container and mutate its element.
var makeCounter = Function():
    var n = 0
    var bump = Function():
        n = n + 1
        return n
    return bump
discard makeCounter()
